    "Both primary sessions used gpt-6.1-sol high. Both direct helper sessions used gpt-6-luna medium, including the landscape follow-up turn.",
    "Both direct spawn calls explicitly requested fork_turns=none, gpt-6-luna and medium effort. Neither helper spawned a descendant.",
    "swarm_primary explicitly cited the native catalog as supporting gpt-6-luna medium before choosing it for small pure-function modules; it retained the more ambiguous hotel logic and integration.",
    "swarm_fitness owned its complete module fixes and focused regression file; swarm_landscape owned its complete module fixes and focused regression file. Primary owned hotel, final FINDINGS.json, integrated tests and report consistency.",
    "Primary detected inaccurate landscape reproduction evidence and requested correction. The landscape helper used original HEAD source to correct the observation in a second turn. That follow-up contributes genuine diagnostic verification work and extra coordination.",
    "Fresh helpers still received repeated runtime and AGENTS instructions. Both re-read README, module source, MAP/TESTING and existing controls; initial-message characters and retained tool-text counts are exposed, not treated as tokenizer-equivalent.",
    "Both runs reported passing all 15 tests and changed-profile verification. Report correctness and defect accuracy are graded separately; passing checks do not prove complete or accurate findings.",
    "Helper initial combined runtime message is 32,868 characters versus primary 4,909\u20134,910; the lower-model helper context therefore has substantial startup instruction footprint. Public counters show input growth despite fresh forks; this is not evidence that parent transcript was inherited."
