  "inferences": [
    "Cheaper native helper models reduce the API-equivalent weight of helper tokens, but do not establish lower subscription usage or faster work. In this run adaptive elapsed time and coding proxy both increased.",
    "This contained task has short modules and limited independent work. Additional helper context, retrieval and correction overlap plausibly account for coordination overhead, but a single pair cannot isolate causal policy effects.",
    "Primary retained useful implementation and integration work rather than merely directing helpers. Exact quality benefit must come from the independent accuracy grading.",
    "Adaptive primary token-price proxy saves only $0.002214 relative to single; helper proxies add $0.01121782, producing $0.00900382 net increase. Thus cheaper helpers nearly offset much larger processed token counts but do not make this run cheaper overall."
